From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:36:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Input: add Novatek NT36523 SPI touchscreen driver

Add a driver for the touchscreen and pen part of the Novatek NT36523
display driver IC over SPI. The controller runs from RAM: each time the
panel is enabled the driver identifies the chip, loads the firmware
named by firmware-name, waits for the firmware to start and enables the
interrupt. It follows the panel through the DRM panel follower API and
starts the firmware after the panel is enabled, with the display already
scanning out. The firmware is loaded again after every panel enable and
after a controller watchdog reset. A reset reported as 0xfe first puts
the MCU in idle and clears its ACI error flag. More than five watchdog
resets in a row, each within ten seconds of the last, stop the reloads
until the panel is enabled again. A start that fails while the panel is
on, for example because the firmware file is not readable yet, is
retried a few times.

After each start the driver sends the pen mode command; the pen module
parameter turns that off.

Touches are reported as a multitouch device with up to ten contacts and
the pen as a separate tablet device with pressure, tilt and two buttons.
Size, orientation and physical size come from the common touchscreen
properties.

Signed-off-by: seilent <github@seilent.net>
